Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 07:59:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] R80b, part 6, patch 1 (cld-advisor, at main's word in M16 and
 M18; main's third folder, section 8, row 4): THE LOCK OF THE PLAN LEAVES THE
 PLAN'S SOURCE AS IT FOUND IT

Sent back with part 1 of this series: B1861's lock, run in one process before tests/test_closure_generated.py,
makes two tests of that file fail. Main's word: a fault of main's lock; a control that changes the builder's
module is to leave it as it found it. The reader of part 1 named six names of the source that the lock leaves
changed.

Made again here, on the commit before this patch: after the lock, two lists of the source hold the same
entries in another order (the nodes of one package; members of the budget). The cause is the undoing of a
control: a name taken out of a list was put back with `append`, at the list's end. The other names the reader
lists point into those two lists. The builder prints in the source's order, so the next file builds another
page than the committed one.

The mend. The source is copied whole when the lock is loaded, after its first build (the builder itself adds
to the source's entries, and that is not undone). Each control puts the source back from that copy, after its
own undoing, and the source is put back after every test of the file. It is put back in place, so that a
name that points into the source points at what it did. A difference of order alone is seen as a difference.

The planted case, in the patch's own test: a name taken out of a list and put back at its end. With that
undoing alone the source differs; put back from the copy, it does not. Also a name added, a name taken, a key
added, a text changed.

Run: the lock and then tests/test_closure_generated.py in one process. On the commit before: 2 failed, 22
passed. On the patch: 25 passed. No test of main's is changed; the helper every control uses gains one line,
with what it was beside it.

Main's fault by main's word; the cause was found by the reader of part 1 and is not checked by main.
